WEBVTT

00:00:02.542 --> 00:00:08.982
<v Angela Zapata>Welcome to the Diploma in Citizen Participation for the Fight against Climate Change.

00:00:09.102 --> 00:00:17.142
This program is an invitation to be an active part of the solution, to become an agent of change in your community.

00:00:17.342 --> 00:00:28.422
Here, you will strengthen your knowledge and skills in mechanisms and strategies that foster a citizenship committed to its environment and its future.

00:00:28.682 --> 00:00:32.462
This Diploma is a fundamental part of the EPAI project.

00:00:32.488 --> 00:00:43.546
Intelligent personal learning environments, funded by the European Union with code EPI 1010-82868.

00:00:43.546 --> 00:00:49.028
It offers you an innovative and high-quality learning experience.

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:58.636
Together we will build a sustainable future, connecting with other citizens passionate about participation and positive impact.

00:00:58.636 --> 00:01:02.378
11 prestigious universities from Latin America and Europe.

00:01:02.656 --> 00:01:09.352
are part of this effort to offer you a cutting-edge learning experience.

00:01:09.352 --> 00:01:21.352
Among the eight participating Latin American universities are the Autonomous Universities of Aguas Calientes and Yucatán in Mexico, the

00:01:21.352 --> 00:01:31.210
American and Technological La Salle Universities of Nicaragua, the National Federico Villarreal and Catholic Santa María Universities of Peru.

00:01:31.959 --> 00:01:38.422
and the National Pedagogical University and the Rafael Núñez University Corporation of Colombia.

00:01:38.523 --> 00:01:42.684
The latter acting as the general coordinator of the project.

00:01:42.685 --> 00:01:54.751
From Europe, we have valuable participation from the Nova University of Lisbon, Portugal, the National Distance Education University (UNED) of Spain, and the

00:01:54.751 --> 00:01:57.732
Technological University of Bucharest in Romania.

00:01:57.973 --> 00:02:00.864
The EPAI project addressing

00:02:00.878 --> 00:02:09.618
the global need to fight against climate change that impacts all people and all living beings on the planet.

00:02:09.618 --> 00:02:20.258
For us humans, in all our areas of development, it creates the opportunity to be agents of change, contributing to training in strategies that promote

00:02:20.258 --> 00:02:27.218
active citizen participation from different levels of the fight against this phenomenon of climate change.

00:02:27.318 --> 00:02:30.676
The general objective of this diploma is to train

00:02:30.676 --> 00:02:43.713
agents of change with competencies and citizen participation in environmental sustainability through active methodologies and the strategic use of digital tools.

00:02:44.053 --> 00:02:57.181
Through project-based learning, participants will be trained to understand the fundamentals of climate change, analyze mechanisms of citizen participation that

00:02:57.181 --> 00:02:59.786
favor environmental sustainability

00:02:59.786 --> 00:03:02.887
through successful cases and initiatives.

00:03:02.947 --> 00:03:13.410
Develop practical activities in the application of digital tools and collaborative strategies with local governments and NGOs for climate action.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:25.933
Design and implement effective communication and environmental education strategies that raise awareness and mobilize the entire community around the actions we can

00:03:25.933 --> 00:03:28.454
develop to mitigate climate change.

00:03:29.002 --> 00:03:42.878
in evaluating public policies and environmental management routes that can be strengthened and with which we can help strengthen the capacity and incidence

00:03:42.878 --> 00:03:46.269
of citizens in actions against this phenomenon.

00:03:46.449 --> 00:03:58.534
Progressively build a differential project, formulating a local or global action plan that involves the community in mitigation and climate adaptation activities.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:12.940
It will also promote the development of competencies such as adopting a sustainability-centered mindset, that sustainability that we must make livable in our daily

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:24.741
lives with each of our actions, recognizing that we have an individual but also collective responsibility to protect and restore that natural environment at the

00:04:24.741 --> 00:04:26.314
local and global level.

00:04:26.314 --> 00:04:32.136
and also to inspire others through the actions we carry out.

00:04:32.296 --> 00:04:42.651
Also to understand the repercussions of climate change on biodiversity and on the living conditions of plants and animals and also on the

00:04:42.651 --> 00:04:45.402
quality of water and air.

00:04:45.542 --> 00:04:56.206
Develop related capacities, develop capacities that are related to the ability to process and use knowledge and information

00:04:56.672 --> 00:05:04.604
of transversal importance and that favor our formation as citizens aware of environmental sustainability.

00:05:04.624 --> 00:05:17.998
And finally, that we contribute to the generation of an awareness in which we recognize that the response to climate change mitigation lies in each of us, that we are

00:05:17.998 --> 00:05:25.738
citizens of the world, local citizens and global citizens, where an excellent starting point

00:05:25.738 --> 00:05:33.369
is to take this diploma, a diploma in which experts will be our teachers.

00:05:33.369 --> 00:05:34.630
Thank you very much.


